1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,076
The disagreement began in the lab, over a cake.

2
00:00:03,076 --> 00:00:11,665
A classmate had brought it to the cafe, and the merriment faded when Maya said that the bakery case was not evidence.

3
00:00:11,665 --> 00:00:16,620
“You cannot ignore the qualitative difference,” she said.

4
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:27,279
“A comparison is not an experiment.” Lin disagreed: an experiment, he argued, needed only one measurable thing.

5
00:00:27,279 --> 00:00:32,958
The milky coffee in front of her went cold while they argued.

6
00:00:32,958 --> 00:00:36,907
Their argument grew comparative and then personal.

7
00:00:36,907 --> 00:00:41,192
“You are ashamed of the messy part,” she said.

8
00:00:41,192 --> 00:00:49,816
“You would rather pose as a scientist than investigate like one.” He heard the injustice in it and said nothing.

9
00:00:49,816 --> 00:00:57,720
The resentment stood between them for a full minute, and the sunny afternoon outside made it worse.

10
00:00:57,720 --> 00:01:09,963
The president of the student union proposed a compromise: a sample in the grocery, a survey in the warehouse, and a small study in the realm of the desirable.

11
00:01:09,963 --> 00:01:13,938
“That is not inclusive,” Maya said.

12
00:01:13,938 --> 00:01:27,576
“It is merely convenient, and it is not comparable to anything we have already done.” Such a plan would compete with better-funded work and lose, and all of them knew it.

13
00:01:27,576 --> 00:01:33,526
The widespread heating failure that week settled the argument by removing the choice.

14
00:01:33,526 --> 00:01:38,210
Half the group was sick; the other half was behind.

15
00:01:38,210 --> 00:01:43,984
“It is advisable to finish this in the warmer months,” the president said.

16
00:01:43,984 --> 00:01:57,278
“Here, in this form, it is merely a guess.” He did not apologize, and she did not apologise either; both were too tired for the ceremony of it.

17
00:01:57,278 --> 00:02:03,038
The compromise was honorable, though the coffee was not.

18
00:02:03,038 --> 00:02:11,412
They inquired, they enquired, they clarified, and eventually they produced an argumentation they could both sign.

19
00:02:11,412 --> 00:02:20,740
It was methodical, respectful, and insightful about its own limits, and it dealt honestly with the dealing of the previous month.

20
00:02:20,740 --> 00:02:25,900
Her curiosity had survived the month, and so had his.

21
00:02:25,900 --> 00:02:29,950
“Not one notable finding,” Lin admitted.

22
00:02:29,950 --> 00:02:32,589
“No,” she said.

23
00:02:32,589 --> 00:02:35,189
“The commencement of a method.

24
00:02:35,189 --> 00:02:46,423
That is all, and that is much.” Their universe was one library, one lab, and one cafe, and the problem was still the same one.

25
00:02:46,423 --> 00:02:57,957
“Regardless,” she added, “the numbers went up in the right direction.” An inquisitive mind, he decided, was not a weakness.

26
00:02:57,957 --> 00:03:09,624
This was the first thing they had grown together rather than by accident, and his major, he realised, had taught him only half of it.
